+Use case: stylized-concept
+Asset type: transparent pixel-art overworld landmark sprite proposal for a north-up Game Boy Advance style Taichung RPG.
+Primary request: generate ONE new National Taiwan Museum of Fine Arts building sprite with one SMALL OPTIONAL DETACHED red angular sculpture sprite beside it on the same transparent canvas. This is an architecture/composition proposal, not a generic monster gym.
+Input images: Image1 official photo = reference for broad rectilinear stone museum mass and the optional red angular lawn sculpture. Image2 official photo = reference for the long dark glazed visitor frontage and thin projecting glass/metal canopy on slender supports. Images3 and4 approved Station/Miyahara studies = pixel-art rendering style ONLY; do not borrow their historic architecture, red brick, pitched roofs, arches, clock towers or grand entrance pillars.
+Subject: a broad LOW horizontal, flat-roofed museum, natural warm gray/taupe stone-clad rectilinear upper mass, a few large dark openings, continuous dark entrance/glazing band, very THIN projecting canopy with a restrained regular rhythm of slender supports. Preserve the real museum's quiet modern proportions and low mass. Stone reads as a few simple tonal groups, not photographic speckle. No grand colonnade or temple/gym silhouette.
+Composition: horizontal front faces south, roof depth visible from the standard north-up RPG three-quarter top-down view; vertical facade lines stay vertical and main frontage stays horizontal, no strong isometric rotation. One centered ground-level entrance legible at game scale. Proposed museum logical facade about192x128 pixels; draw a crisp nearest-neighbor enlarged6x preview on a1152x768 canvas. Broad museum facade dominates the width; keep low silhouette and modest roof depth, with clean transparent margins. Place the optional sculpture as a small independent red bent/angular geometric prop near the lower-left side, separated from all museum pixels by visible transparent space, no overlap, no plinth/lawn patch, at most one-sixth the building width. It is not roof ornament and not a monument as tall as the museum.
+Style: hand-placed hard square pixel clusters, clear stepped silhouettes, bold but restrained dark outline, readable GBA-scale materials matching the approved style references. Limited intended14 opaque colors plus transparency: warm stone shades, deep blue-charcoal glazing, muted canopy gray, and2 red sculpture tones; no smooth gradients, no painted blur, no microtexture, no antialiasing.
+Background: genuine transparent RGBA, binary alpha0/255, no drop-shadow glow or translucent shadow haze. No floor, lawn, backdrop, streets, trees, water, landscape, crowds, people, vehicles, banners, labels, text, logos, gym badges or map UI. Sculpture and facade must both be isolated against true transparency. Deliver ONE composition only, not a sheet of variations or a labeled presentation board.
+Implementation boundary: current game entrance10,62 / approach10,63 / arrival10,65 stay unchanged for later Main fitting. Do not draw coordinate labels or imply a final map footprint. This output is proposed artwork only; exact palette count, transparency and logical-grid compliance will be measured afterwards.
