+# Fine Arts Museum: next architecture reference brief
+
+Architecture remains open for user review. This reference brief does not approve a facade, sculpture, footprint or palette.
+
+The inspected official gallery shows a broad, rectilinear stone-clad block, large dark openings and a long glazed visitor frontage beneath a thin projecting canopy. The open sculpture lawn is a useful identity cue; one photograph shows a prominent red angular sculpture. The museum's own architectural-history leaflet also records changes to entrances and circulation, so historical entrance imagery should not silently replace the gallery's later facade.
+
+At native scale, preserve the long stone mass, dark entrance band and canopy depth. Suggest stone with a few tonal groups rather than photographic speckle. Reduce canopy supports and glazing to a regular readable rhythm. Omit temporary exhibition banners and tiny building lettering. A sculpture, if chosen, should be a separate lawn prop with its own clear silhouette, not decoration invented on the roof.
+
+**First focused decision:** show the museum facade with one detached sculpture, or the facade alone? The facade-plus-sculpture composition is the recommendation for review; the user has not selected it. The exact sculpture and lawn placement remain open.
+
+The Greenway gym door stays **(10,62)**, approach **(10,63)** and arrival **(10,65)**. The current placeholder [5,56,15,62] does not allocate final art size or a graphics bank.
+
+Sources and photo credit: [Taichung Tourism exterior gallery](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/intro/901), [official architecture description](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/experience/culture), and the [museum's architectural-history leaflet](https://event.culture.tw/userFiles/NTMOFA/DownloadFile/01/90143/01/90143_00.pdf). Photo URLs/hashes are in `references-next.json`. No photograph or sculpture asset is copied into the game.
