@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: a single original Game Boy Advance / FireRed-style overworld landmark building cutout, an art study for future native tile conversion.
+
+Input image 1 is the official frontal photograph of OLD TAICHUNG STATION and is the architecture reference. Follow its real building identity: a tall central CLOCK TOWER with a white circular clock face and small oxidized dark-green spire, a decorative raised central gable, a tall central arched glass window, red brick with cream-white stone bands and pilasters, symmetric low wings with repeated arched windows, broad SLATE / CHARCOAL hipped roofs, and a low olive-gray entrance canopy. Simplify tiny ornament while preserving this silhouette and these distinguishing features.
+
+Input image 2 is a native FireRed game screenshot. Use ONLY its crisp pixel rendering and north-up overworld perspective / roof depth as style guidance. Do not copy the screenshot's generic museum building, pink roof, trees, paving, character, or composition.
+
+Create ONE south-facing station building, with its front facade horizontal and centered. Use the ordinary FireRed overworld view: see the facade and some roof from above, orthographic and aligned to a square grid, with no diagonal isometric rotation or vanishing-point perspective. Keep the full clock tower, roofs and both low wings visible and uncropped. No additional floors or towers.
+
+The target logical sprite is exactly192×128 pixels, a12×8 grid of16-pixel metatiles. If possible output a1536×1024 canvas showing that logical sprite at exactly8× integer enlargement: every logical pixel should be an8×8 hard-edged square. The base entrance sits in the bottom metatile row7; the central visual opening spans logical metatile columns5–6, with future active door on the right column6. Keep the building base aligned across the image near its bottom edge. No drawn grid or coordinate labels.
+
+Use crisp flat pixel clusters, economical dark outlines, simple two- or three-tone shading from upper left, a restrained palette of roughly24 opaque colors, rusty brick reds, warm cream stone, charcoal-blue slate, desaturated blue glass, a muted olive-gray canopy, and a small dark-green clock-tower cap. Preserve true transparency outside the building, including above and beside the clock-tower silhouette. Alpha should be hard edged; do not draw a checkerboard.
+
+The output contains the building only. No ground, pavement, grass, trees, people, vehicles, signs, posters, logos, text, labels, UI, watermark, detached cast shadow, scenery, or decorative frame. No red roof, added domes, fantasy castle towers, painterly texture, gradients, antialiasing, blur, photorealism, or smooth vector illustration.
