+# Science Museum: next architecture reference brief
+
+The user selected the main exhibition entrance. Its eventual facade artwork remains open for review. This is a reference brief, with no art generation or native allocation.
+
+The official gallery shows two distinct identities. The exhibition entrance is a low, gray, rectilinear composition with a deep central recess, slim entrance supports and dark horizontal window bands. The Botanical Garden glasshouse is a separate tall, curved glass structure with pronounced light ribs. Both photographs were inspected; they should not be fused into an invented building.
+
+For the exhibition facade, preserve the recessed entry and broad horizontal proportions. Reduce the stone surface to a few flat tones and the windows to clear dark bands; omit exhibition banners, tiny lettering, traffic and crowds. For a glasshouse alternative, prioritize the outline and several structural ribs over every pane. Follow the approved north-up frontal overworld treatment with visible roof depth.
+
+**Selected direction:** the user chose the main exhibition entrance with its broad gray facade and recessed entry. Keep the separate Botanical Garden glasshouse out of this first gym facade. Artwork, footprint and palette remain unapproved.
+
+The existing Greenway contract stays fixed: door **(24,20)**, approach **(24,21)**, arrival **(24,23)**. The current placeholder footprint is [19,14,29,20]; it is not an approved bespoke-art envelope or budget.
+
+Sources and photo credit: [Taichung Tourism museum gallery](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/Attractions/Intro/1691), [distinct Botanical Garden reference](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/intro/902), and the [museum's own facility map](https://www.nmns.edu.tw/ch/exhibitions/galleries/floor/1f/index.html). Specific inspected photo URLs and hashes are in `references-next.json`. Photographs remain reference material, not game textures.
