+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: ONE proposed landmark sprite study for a north-up GBA-style Taichung city overworld.
+
+Primary request: a compact two-dormitory courtyard cluster that reads as Shen Ji New Village / 審計新村, based on the two official reference photos. This is a proposed composition for architecture review, not a final map installation.
+
+Input images: Image1 is the official village/massing photograph and Image2 the official gable/exterior-stair photograph. Follow their actual architecture: modest weathered cream plaster, two stories, red/orange tiled gabled roofs, plain rectangular brown-framed windows, simple gray bases and the rhythm of small converted dormitories. Image3 is an approved high-resolution Old Station study used ONLY for pixel rendering and the shared frontal north-up game-art treatment. Do not copy its station geometry, clock, tower, monumental symmetry, brick facade, slate roof, canopy or soft glow.
+
+Composition: show exactly two compact dormitory buildings with a narrow pedestrian gap/courtyard opening between them. Keep both on a horizontal south/front baseline, with the complete silhouettes visible. One building can show a frontal triangular gable; the second can show a slightly longer dormitory frontage and the same red/orange roof family. Use only a small amount of visible roof depth. A simple attached exterior stair may appear on the secondary building if it remains legible, as verified in Image2. No invented bridge, arch, third building or extra floor. Make the gap transparent through to the lower edge so underlying native ground can later supply the walking lane. No painted ground.
+
+Gym entry: one clearly readable south-facing dark doorway on the main left dormitory, near its side adjoining the courtyard gap. Prefer its center near logical x68 and the bottom row of a nominal192x128 canvas, leaving a clear approach beneath. The secondary building's ground-level openings should read as windows or closed shop panels, not another emphasized gym entrance. No sign, icon, badge, lettering or UI to mark the door. Exact native geometry is unapproved and will be reconciled later.
+
+Projection and scale: orthographic frontal north-up RPG overworld, vertical walls vertical and front baseline horizontal, slight roof depth like a FireRed city facade. No rotated45-degree isometric view, dramatic camera perspective or dollhouse cutaway. Nominal logical192x128 pixels, enlarged integer8x onto1536x1024 if possible. Coherent bold pixel clusters and simple reusable window/roof rhythms matter more than tiny photo details.
+
+Materials and style: warm cream/light-yellow plaster with restrained gray weathering, terracotta/orange-red roofs, dark brown window frames, muted cool glass and a dark outline. Aim for no more than14 opaque flat color shades plus transparency. Hard pixel edges and readable small-scale shapes. Minimal roof-tile marks, no random grain, no fine speckled texture, no gradients, no antialiasing, no blur, no glow, no painterly or smooth3D rendering. Neutral daylight.
+
+Background: TRUE transparent alpha outside buildings and through the courtyard gap; hard binary alpha, not a checkerboard or colored backdrop. No scenery, paving, floor, cast-ground shadow, trees, plants, people, market stalls, umbrellas, cars, air-conditioning units, posters, logos, text, murals, watermarks or surrounding city buildings. In particular OMIT the large blue illustrated mural from Image2; keep that wall as the verified cream-plaster architectural mass. Produce one complete proposed cluster only.
