@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# National Taichung Theater: second landmark study
+
+Status: a photo-referenced study for focused review. This package does not change
+the current game map or register native graphic tiles. Old Station's native
+conversion remains a separate workstream owned by Root.
+
+The recognizable feature is the building's broad rectangular mass combined with
+curved concrete/glass fields that pinch into hourglass and bottle-like profiles.
+The official complete exterior photo supplies that arrangement. The daylight
+close-up clarifies light concrete, cool shadows, blue-gray glass and thin dark
+glazing bars. An architectural interior photograph was also inspected to understand
+the sound-cave curves, but is not a generation input and should not turn the whole
+facade into an interior cave.
+
+The accepted Station study supplies the visual family only. No clock, brick,
+hipped roof, extra tower, dome or generic gym facade belongs on this theater.
+The image should use the game's north-up, south-facing facade with visible roof
+depth; the official photos' oblique camera angles are reference information.
+
+## Shape and material priorities
+
+Preserve the straight outer mass and flat roof boundary, large central pinched
+glass field, curved side openings and recessed cave identity. Keep the uneven
+rhythm of the actual facade instead of repeating identical arched windows. A few
+small breathing-hole accents are enough at game resolution. Daylight concrete
+uses warm ivory highlights and cool gray shading, with desaturated blue glass and
+charcoal-blue glazing bars. These forms have higher priority than tiny ornament.
+
+The study excludes the real plaza, fountain, skyline, greenery, people and signs.
+Those are separate map-fill assets. It requests true transparency, hard alpha,
+flat pixel shading and no halo, with economical outlines in the same family as
+the Station study. The exact built-in image generation prompt is versioned as
+`generation-prompt.txt`; its complete input provenance is in `references.json`.
+
+## Baseline entrance and envelope
+
+The art proposal is16×10 metatiles /256×160 logical pixels. At origin(4,35), its
+south-facing door local(8,9) preserves the current global(12,44) in
+`MAP_TAICHUNG_XITUN`, warp2/elevation0. Keep the southern approach(12,45) and safe
+arrival(12,47) clear at elevation3. The current gym ID and three return warps are
+unchanged. The larger visual opening may span columns7–8 while the existing right
+door remains the only active baseline warp.
+
+This envelope is an art-sizing proposal, not approved native placement. Its north
+rows35–38 overlap part of the baseline Maple Garden east-west street. Root must
+reconcile the footprint, roof layering, paths and collisions before registration.
+The future expanded city has a separately versioned placement contract; its game
+coordinates are not set by this proposal. No collision cells are reserved here.
+
+## Native encoding target
+
+Use the immutable General primary graphics for common ground and service tiles.
+A provisional target is at most256 unique8×8 theater graphics, leaving128 of the
+384 secondary slots for shared neighborhood assets; repeat glazing bars and flat
+concrete patches wherever possible. The160-cell envelope needs at most160 new
+metatile definitions before reuse. Target at most three16-entry4bpp palette banks;
+Root assigns actual bank IDs against the shared city kit. These are budgets to
+measure during packing, not claims about the generated image.
+
+Suggested material families are ivory(240,240,232), cool concrete(208,216,216),
+shadow(168,184,192), light glass(160,208,224), mid glass(96,160,184), deep glass
+(48,104,144) and charcoal frames(40,64,80). They are production suggestions rounded
+to GBA-friendly multiples of8, not sampled measurements from the photographs.
+
+Maintain the native animated-door behavior and explicit animation mapping. A
+custom painted door does not automatically define its opening frames. Confirm
+collision, clear approaches, interior entry, return and transport arrival in the
+actual ROM after the final asset is registered.
+
+## Review and conversion state
+
+The first built-in call has produced `theater-study-v1.png` in the isolated
+`landmark-art` artifacts directory. Its large curved glass/concrete fields and
+rectangular mass follow the selected reference. It remains a study, with
+`nativeReady=false`. Root can show this one landmark immediately as an independent
+review item; it does not wait for other streams or authorize other landmark art.
+
+`generation.json` records the actual raster dimensions, alpha, palette/grid
+measurements and remaining conversion checks. It must not be presented as a
+native game screenshot or a tile-ready asset before those checks succeed.
+
+The first output measures1536×1024 rather than the requested1536×960, so its height
+is not divisible by the requested6× logical pixel scale. It contains673,880 fully
+transparent pixels, but also255 alpha levels,898,984 partially transparent pixels,
+60,583 distinct visible RGBA values and a soft halo. None of25,477 complete aligned
+6×6 blocks containing visible pixels is uniform. These failures keep native
+readiness false even though the basic facade identity is recognizable. Simplified
+roof furniture also needs final reference review. No extra redraw, creative raster
+edit or native registration was performed in this milestone.
+
+## Approved direction and native-size encoding candidate
+
+The user approved this silhouette with “Use this direction”. Architectural shape
+review is complete for this pass. A deterministic encoding candidate is now in
+`candidate/`; the high-resolution study is preserved unchanged. It was converted
+with `encode_candidate.py`, with no new image generation or creative redraw.
+
+The candidate uses a hard alpha threshold of224, an aspect-preserving crop fitted
+to the south edge of a256×160 envelope, nearest sampling, uniform2×2 native-pixel
+clusters, and14 opaque GBA-rounded colors in candidate palette7. It is a true indexed
+4bpp asset with binary alpha and a verified flip-aware tilemap round-trip. A4×
+nearest preview is saved as `landmark-art/theater-native-candidate-v1.png`.
+
+Its319 unique8×8 graphics exceed the initial256-art target, so the actual scene was
+measured instead of assuming the entire prefab catalog is required. After removing
+only the old Theater facade, baseline Xitun requires20 raw secondary graphics,
+or18 after flip deduplication. The actual union is337/384 graphics, leaving47 slots.
+Remaining baseline palette banks are0,1,2,3,5,8,9; candidate palette7 is free. Keeping
+the79 existing secondary metatile IDs and appending all160 candidate cells uses
+239/384 definitions. `analyze_bank.py` and `candidate/integration-budget.json`
+record these read-only measurements and source hashes.
+
+The fitted building is256×110 pixels at offset(0,50), leaving its first three
+metatile rows fully transparent. This reduces the original north-street concern;
+Root still determines actual collision and restores the old facade's background.
+The painted central entrance spans columns7–8 at the south edge. Root binds the
+right cell(8,9) to the existing door(12,44), with approach/arrival unchanged, and
+tests its animation and return. Palette assignment, shared-bank registration and
+ROM checks are pending, so overall `nativeReady` remains false. No240-pixel variant
+was necessary because the approved256-pixel candidate fits the actual bank.
