@@ -0,0 +1,193 @@
+# City v2 geography: sourced first-review layer
+
+This is the geography workstream's input to the larger city, prepared on
+7 November 2026. It supplies actual road geometry, a provisional section grid,
+neighborhood fill roles, unpainted lots and landmark sizing conflicts. It does
+not register native maps, move doors, change gameplay, or replace the current
+playable city. The ten approved landmarks remain the ten gym anchors.
+
+## Review outputs
+
+- `docs/city-v2-streets.json`: machine-readable source/draft contract, about2.8MB.
+  Inspect selected fields with Python rather than dumping the entire file.
+- `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/geography/city-v2-street-draft.png`: actual
+  municipal street centerlines beneath the16-section planning overlay.
+- `tools/taichung/geography/build_draft.py`: reproducible clipping, reprojection,
+  source selection, section/port, reserve and empty-lot generator.
+- `tools/taichung/geography/validate_draft.py`: source/placement separation,
+  native-ID preservation, section-buffer and reciprocal-port checks.
+- `tools/taichung/geography/fetch_government_catalog.py`: fetches the public
+  catalog and records the specific archive links and optional local hashes.
+- `tools/taichung/geography/fetch_osm.py`: optional read-only OSM fetch helper;
+  the Overpass services were unavailable during this pass and are not the data
+  source for the current street preview.
+
+## Actual source and provenance
+
+The main source is Taichung City Government's
+[114-year road-survey dataset 177459](https://data.gov.tw/en/datasets/177459),
+published 20 April 2026 and updated 4 June 2026 in the source portal. It provides
+road centerlines, road surfaces and special transport surfaces at 1:1000 survey
+scale. The 114-year label refers to the 2025 survey edition; this is not a claim
+that every road was surveyed on the 2026 retrieval date.
+
+The [public catalog CSV](https://newdatacenter.taichung.gov.tw/api/v1/no-auth/resource.download?rid=e57517f7-f405-4e24-bd03-c4b354dcecfe)
+points to the exact archives used:
+
+- [R0002 road centerlines](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZoTu4rS3C9PHZ_ZMdFhfm_YphjLDb3VI/view):
+  `114期末_R0002_1226 (2).7z`,15,289,661 bytes; provider modification time
+  `2026-03-25T09:09:54.404Z`.
+- [R0004 special transport surfaces](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1P9N8wCtLxbEkDwwS6_k4ieMctuI0Vs9f/view):
+  `114期末_R0004_1106.7z`,450,265 bytes. These polygons are mostly unnamed and
+  are not assumed to be railway corridors or walkable roads.
+- [Official field codebook](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zfgkKIEb0A3J6tG7HbTQdugA6ciLpKK6/view):
+  confirms `R2B` road name, `R2C` district, `R2J` total width, `R2S` road type,
+  `R2D/E` alley/sub-alley and `R2L` update year.
+
+The specific public Drive IDs were retrieved read-only with the Google Drive
+connector. Archives, exact hashes, modification/retrieval timestamps and the
+codebook text are preserved under the isolated `geography/` artifact directory;
+no authenticated download URL is retained in provenance. The portal publishes
+the Open Government Data License, version 1.0. Attribution is Taichung City
+Government.
+
+The Shapefile's own `.prj` identifies TWD97 TM2 zone 121, matching EPSG 3826.
+`pyproj.Transformer` converts it to EPSG 4326/WGS84 using `always_xy=True`.
+Actual geometry is clipped to bounds before projection; out-of-bounds points
+are never clamped into invented lines along the map edge.
+
+The existing official tourism pin catalog supplies nine approved points. Its
+older saved `map.json` did not yet contain Maple Garden, so that tenth point is
+loaded directly from official tourism dataset 7777 record
+`Attraction_387000000A_000818`: longitude 120.63935, latitude 24.16801. Excluded
+Gaomei, Dajia Temple, Luce Chapel and Dakeng are not imported as gym anchors.
+
+Section-center district labels reuse the existing township-boundary artifact,
+whose provenance records the 2011 boundary dataset via
+[twgeojson](https://github.com/ronnywang/twgeojson). They provide coarse planning
+context rather than current cadastral or land-use zoning; each road also retains
+its district field from the newer municipal survey.
+
+## Scale and street selection
+
+Bounds are longitude 120.62–120.72 and latitude 24.11–24.20, roughly 10×10 km of
+central urban Taichung. The raw projection is 256×256 metatiles split into a 4×4
+grid of 64×64 sections:65,536 outdoor cells, approximately 7.88 times the current
+8,320-cell three-area blockout. This remains a sizing assumption for review.
+Every 64×64 section needs 6,162 virtual-buffer cells with the existing native
+15/14 padding, below the10,240-cell limit.
+
+The archive has 130,189 road records citywide. After exact clipping, the draft
+retains 25,445 unique survey records as preview/source context, producing 25,707
+polyline parts. The selected, readable game-backbone input is 2,395 parts across
+159 named roads. Selection uses actual total width ≥30 m, selected named avenues
+and gym-frontage streets, or surveyed dedicated cycle corridors. Named spine
+selection excludes alleys/sub-alleys so each named arterial does not bring all
+its small branches into the game. Full source detail remains in the archive.
+
+Examples include Taiwan Boulevard, Wenxin, Gongyi, Wuquan, Xiangshang, Zhongqing,
+Chongde, Fuxing, Jianguo, plus local gym approaches such as Wenhua/Fuxing streets,
+Huilai, Guanqian, Minsheng and Zhongshan. Original Chinese names are retained;
+missing English names are not fabricated. Parallel carriageways and small survey
+segments still need merging/simplification during authored game-route placement.
+
+The draft has 93 source-derived seam candidates,92 potentially suitable for a
+player street. These are individual road crossings, not93 native connection
+records. Adjacent sections can share one reciprocal map connection with several
+street openings. Ports provide matching local 63/0 edge cells, reciprocal
+directions and offset 0 for the aligned64×64 grid. Crossings near corners are
+explicitly adjusted to leave room for the sidewalk/road width. Elevated/freeway
+features remain flagged for grade review; a visual line crossing is not proof
+of a walking junction.
+
+## City fill beyond the gyms
+
+Eleven of the sixteen sections contain no selected gym. Their proposed fill
+recipes include residential/retail streets and ordinary urban blocks around
+Xitun, Beitun, North, Nantun, South and East areas; the southeast edge reaches
+Taiping under this provisional bounding box.
+
+Background colors in the preview are authored game fill proposals, not surveyed
+zoning. The 102 empty candidate lots avoid the selected road corridors and gym
+sizing reserves: 83 prefer 12×8 envelopes and 19 use 8×8 fallback envelopes where
+the wider size does not fit. Scan spacing keeps these candidates from overlapping.
+They have no source building ID, prefab selection or painted
+metatiles. Some omitted real minor streets may be absorbed into a larger game
+block deliberately. The fill owner chooses compatible normal-building/prop
+modules and applies their paint, solid and mandatory-clear masks after the next
+placement pass; actual buildings are not inferred from road voids as source truth.
+
+## Real GPS points are not game entrances
+
+Every landmark retains three separate concepts: real WGS84 position, raw
+projected sizing point, and an unassigned authored game entrance. Its existing
+native map 43 exterior/door/arrival/interior reference is copied unchanged for
+integration compatibility. No projected point is silently promoted to a door.
+
+The draft reserves an artwork footprint plus a four-tile southern apron and a
+two-tile clearance check. Uniform scaling exposes four conflicts:
+
+| Pair | Raw projected point distance | Required follow-up |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Station / Miyahara |4.78 tiles | Locally expand the arrival cluster |
+| Greenway / Shen Ji |11.35 tiles | Separate art/apron reserves while retaining neighborhood proximity |
+| Shen Ji / Fine Arts Museum |10.64 tiles | Expand the arts corridor enough for both buildings and approaches |
+| Theater / Maple Garden |15.44 tiles | Separate the larger landscape/art reserves |
+
+Those are sizing studies, not approved relocation coordinates. Preserve the
+real source graph and use local elastic game placement to resolve the conflicts.
+The current native Station (32,64), approach(32,65) and spawn(30,66) remain valid
+until Main and the mapping integrator publish a versioned replacement contract.
+
+## Missing layers and honest limits
+
+Actual railway centerlines, waterway traces and building footprints/land-use
+zoning were not retrieved for this first pack. The initial Overpass endpoint
+failed TLS/HTTP access checks; the documented alternative returned HTTP504 and a
+single-road probe timed out. No rail or river paths were guessed. R0004's
+unnamed transport polygons are carried only as unclassified source context.
+
+This source-derived map is not yet traversable native geography. Road corridor
+widths, four-direction simplification, bridges/elevation, merged ports, local
+streets, collision, habitat polygons, art/prefab placement and arrivals require
+composition followed by native build/runtime checks. The current city/gyms,
+language/starter flow and save behavior are unaffected by these new files.
+
+## Reproduce and validate
+
+Use Python3.11 or newer and install `requirements.txt` into an isolated environment. The completed run used
+`geography/python-deps/` under the artifact namespace, leaving system packages and
+the source checkout untouched.
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/taichung/geography/fetch_government_catalog.py \
+  --output-dir /path/to/geography \
+  --road-archive /path/to/taichung-centerlines-114.7z
+
+# Retrieve the exact public archive IDs above, then extract into artifact dirs.
+# Supply the source .shp, official tourism/boundary artifacts and baseline contract.
+python3 tools/taichung/geography/build_draft.py \
+  --roads /path/to/114期末_R0002_1226.shp \
+  --transport /path/to/114期末_R0004_1106.shp \
+  --landmarks /path/to/map-data/map.json \
+  --attractions /path/to/map-data/attractions.json \
+  --townships /path/to/map-data/townships.geojson \
+  --baseline-contract docs/taichung-city-contract.json \
+  --source-metadata /path/to/geography/catalog-download-metadata.json \
+  --output docs/city-v2-streets.json \
+  --preview /path/to/geography/city-v2-street-draft.png
+
+python3 tools/taichung/geography/validate_draft.py
+```
+
+Draft validation passes for sixteen section capacities, all ten preserved gym
+IDs/door anchors, source clipping bounds, source/game-coordinate separation,
+reciprocal seam candidate coordinates and unpainted lots. Additional geometry
+probes passed: fully outside lines remain outside, clipped crossing lines keep
+correct endpoints, near-collinear simplification is bounded, and the future
+four-direction raster helper produces only Manhattan-adjacent steps.
+
+The source preview was visually inspected. Roads are the actual city survey,
+the ten gym pins/reserves and16 sections are readable, and missing layers and
+reserve conflicts are explicitly labeled. No native source registration or ROM
+build is claimed by this geography-only handoff.
