+# Neighborhood character inputs
+
+The approved 16-section grid now has distinct ordinary-neighborhood profiles.
+They describe the intended mix of housing, commerce, apparent age, building mass,
+street frontage, planting and roof families. Main retail frontages and residential
+side streets have separate overrides inside every section. The first native fill
+study can continue from the approved R2C2 old-core profile independently of the
+other fifteen sections.
+
+`data/taichung/neighborhoods/profiles.json` is the background assembler input.
+`evidence.json` records the primary sources, their dates, their geographic scope,
+access limitations and the limits of each interpretation. All numerical mixtures
+and densities are **authored game targets**, not measured shares of real parcels,
+zoning, construction years or population density. The section's administrative
+district is recorded at its center only; sections can cross district boundaries.
+
+## Section character
+
+The percentages below are authoring targets for ordinary infill after roads,
+arrivals and landmark reserves. They are not a new area-wide approval queue.
+Review continues in independently useful blocks and sections.
+
+| Section | Intended ordinary city character | Housing / retail-food target | Older / contemporary style target | Source-to-section confidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| R0C0 | Northwest Xitun local housing, shops and services | 65 / 17% | 30 / 20% | Low; beyond the directly documented market core |
+| R0C1 | Fengjia student-market frontages, housing behind them | 42 / 40% | 32 / 15% | High for broad market character |
+| R0C2 | North Beitun redevelopment mixed with older pockets | 70 / 12% | 18 / 50% | Medium; scheme boundary is not a building inventory |
+| R0C3 | Songzhu east-side housing and local services | 72 / 12% | 22 / 30% | Low; provisional ordinary fabric |
+| R1C0 | Theater/Maple Garden commercial, residential and park cluster | 42 / 22% | 8 / 70% | High for cluster; visual modernity is authored |
+| R1C1 | Museum node with mature mixed-use residential streets | 48 / 26% | 24 / 20% | Medium beyond the cultural node |
+| R1C2 | North District mature housing and service strips | 63 / 19% | 38 / 14% | Medium broad character; age lead is historical and partial |
+| R1C3 | Taiyuan east everyday housing and small services | 70 / 14% | 26 / 24% | Low; targeted street references still needed |
+| R2C0 | Gongyi dining fronts and mixed-age Nantun housing | 62 / 22% | 20 / 38% | Medium; old-town identity stays in pockets |
+| R2C1 | Greenway arts/cafes, renovated lanes and ordinary homes | 47 / 25% | 39 / 18% | High for the cultural spine |
+| R2C2 | Station/Central old commercial streets and quieter homes | 40 / 35% | 60 / 8% | High for broad old-core character; approved pilot |
+| R2C3 | East/Taiping housing with limited workshop-history accents | 58 / 14% | 35 / 20% | Low; no current factory/zoning inventory |
+| R3C0 | Southwest Nantun transitional housing and local services | 61 / 13% | 32 / 23% | Low; district history is only broad context |
+| R3C1 | Daqing transition: older pockets, newer massing and open gaps | 67 / 13% | 22 / 40% | Medium; public works completion is not housing completion |
+| R3C2 | Xingda student-food streets and South District homes | 61 / 22% | 33 / 15% | Medium beyond the documented food corridor |
+| R3C3 | Xinren/Taiping ordinary housing and local-service edge | 62 / 14% | 30 / 20% | Low; provisional use/style distribution |
+
+The Fengjia profile follows the district office's description of a university
+shopping area around several named streets. The older Central profile follows
+the city's 2026 street-house repair programme; qualifying buildings must be at
+least thirty years old, but that condition does not date every building in the
+area. Sources: [Fengjia district description](https://www.xitun.taichung.gov.tw/831932/831997/1513668/1514200),
+[old-street repair programme](https://www.ud.taichung.gov.tw/28928/28931/28937/3231245).
+
+The Greenway provides a sourced cultural/open-space spine, while the seventh
+district has a documented cluster of department-store commerce, the Theater and
+nearby parks. The southern Daqing redevelopment supplies context for transition,
+not permission to make every parcel contemporary. Sources:
+[Greenway](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/zh-tw/Attractions/Intro/786/),
+[seventh-district cluster](https://www.taichung.gov.tw/8868/8872/9962/3104993),
+[Daqing public works completion](https://www.taichung.gov.tw/8868/8872/9962/3200714).
+
+No current section-level building-age, height or population-density series was
+obtained. A historical MOI housing-age lead is retained with its access limitation
+and is explicitly excluded from numerical calibration. Road width and source
+segment counts are never used as estimates of housing age, zoning or people.
+Xuefu Road is supported by the South District's student-food description but is
+absent from the selected road extract within R3C2. The profiles disclose that
+omission rather than inventing a road trace or assigning its shops to another
+street as fact.
+
+## Filling coherent blocks
+
+The shared schema uses `authoredVisualTargets` with `useMix`, `ageStyleMix`,
+`heightMix`, `roofColorMix`, frontage, setbacks, arcade/signage frequency, green
+space, coverage and `prefabRoleWeights`. Each normalized mixture sums to one.
+Role names match the existing normal-prefab catalog. `streetBands` provides
+`primaryRetailFrontage` and `residentialSideStreet` overrides.
+
+Choose a dominant roof family, height band and setback for a run of roughly four
+to eight buildings. Place occasional accent roofs within that run, then change
+the dominant treatment at the next block or frontage. Keep local services near
+corners and reserve the denser sign/storefront treatment for selected main-road
+frontages. This creates deliberate local repetition without making a whole
+section homogeneous. Roof family names are art direction, not exact RGB values
+or native palette-bank allocations.
+
+The present catalog partly represents the desired age, arcade and height range.
+The metadata does not claim that high-rise silhouettes, Taiwanese workshops or
+custom arcade art already exist. The assembler must continue to check actual
+module dimensions, allowed context, paint/solid/mandatory-clear masks and dormant
+door rules. It should leave unsupported visual variants explicit rather than
+silently turning every class into the same building.
+
+## Approved old-core pilot
+
+`pilot-profile.json` was delivered first so the color/building stream could start
+immediately. `pilot-r2c2-layout.json` is the approved, isolated 64×64 spatial draft.
+Its source road records and raw projected GPS points remain separate from its
+authored road control points and proposed local gym entrances. Six real road
+names provide a simplified backbone; their authored alignments are locally
+stretched to make room for the facades and ordinary blocks.
+
+Station remains southeast of Miyahara, with the Park to the north. The Station
+and Miyahara reserve envelopes no longer overlap. The layout offers 24 unpainted
+lots of different sizes, each with compatible-size normal-module IDs. The values
+are not source building footprints or a final selection of buildings. Clear
+approaches connect all three proposed south arrivals to one walking network.
+
+| Gym ID | Proposed local art rectangle, inclusive | Proposed local entrance | Proposed local arrival |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `old-taichung-station` | `[44,44,55,51]` | `[50,51]` | `[50,54]` |
+| `miyahara` | `[21,38,30,45]` | `[26,45]` | `[26,48]` |
+| `taichung-park` | `[35,13,50,24]` | `[43,24]` | `[43,27]` |
+
+These coordinates belong to the new pilot only. Original native map43 gym doors,
+warp IDs, return anchors and startup coordinates remain recorded verbatim and
+unchanged. Neighbor seam suggestions are unpaired. The mapping integrator and
+Main must agree the versioned map/door/save contract before native registration.
+Rail geometry, waterway banks and source building footprints remain missing
+layers; none was fabricated for this pilot.
+
+The pilot is frozen for the streetscape worker's approved fill pass. Further
+spatial changes require a separate review item rather than silently changing the
+input being composed. The remaining fifteen profiles are background input and
+do not hold up that pass.
+
+## Reproduce and check
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/geography/profile_character.py \
+  --artifact-dir /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods
+```
+
+This regenerates `profiles.json`, a CSV summary, a 16-card overview PNG and a
+validation report. It verifies section IDs, normalized mixtures, real role names,
+source references and separate retail/residential treatment. Requested named-road
+frontages are checked against source geometry intersecting their section. R2C2
+copies the consumed pilot targets rather than changing them.
+
+The helper requires Pillow from the existing geography requirements. This pack
+was reproduced with `/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3`; the default
+macOS interpreter currently lacks Pillow. `provenance.json` records the tested
+interpreter, exact command and input/output hashes.
+
+The pilot helper, `profile_pilot.py`, separately reproduces its JSON and two-panel
+engineering preview from the fixed authored control points and source street
+draft. It checks road/facade separation, reserve clearance, candidate module sizes,
+one connected walking network and all three arrival connections. Its buffer
+estimate is 6,162 cells against the 10,240-cell native limit. Neither helper
+registers native maps, changes native IDs, paints source maps or builds a ROM.
+
+Artifacts are in
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/`:
+
+- `pilot-r2c2-layout.png` and `pilot-r2c2-validation.json`.
+- `neighborhood-character-overview.png` and `neighborhood-character-summary.csv`.
+- `profiles-validation.json`.
+
+The 16-card overview is an engineering summary for background composition, not a
+request to review sixteen areas together. User review remains focused on each
+independently ready item.
