+# Old Station native asset
+
+The approved architectural study now has a deterministic192×128 indexed source
+in `data/taichung/landmarks/old-station/native.png`. It retains the slate roof,
+cream bands, brick wings, clock tower and canopy. The full-resolution generated
+study remains a reference artifact; it is not the raster loaded by the game.
+
+The conversion uses BOX downsampling, alpha threshold200 and nearest assignment
+to fifteen GBA-aligned colors, with transparent index0. Horizontal/vertical8×8
+tile flips are packed and their native reference flags adjusted. Input hashes,
+actual allocations and palette ownership are recorded in the generated bank's
+`compile-manifest.json` and the Station `placement.json`.
+
+## Native placement and bank
+
+Only OldCity switches to `gTileset_TaichungOldCity`. The new secondary bank keeps
+all44 original metatile IDs used by the baseline exterior and complete normal
+prefab library. Those IDs also cover both other baseline districts. Original
+General/Pewter graphics and palettes are unchanged. General still supplies640
+primary graphics, ground and the animated door.
+
+The secondary allocation is64 shared source graphics plus225 Station graphics:
+289 unique tiles, or304 including PNG row padding, within384 hardware slots.
+Door animation reserves the last eight graphic slots(1016–1023), leaving376
+usable scene slots:87 before row padding, or72 immediately free after padding.
+The Station uses palette7; palette12 remains reserved for neighborhood colorways.
+The measured225 is one tile above the initial224 target, accommodated by the
+shared source bank's flip deduplication. The provisional two-palette allowance
+was reduced to one palette. Source palettes8–11 remain intact.
+
+The12×8 envelope starts at(26,57). The door remains(32,64), approach(32,65),
+arrival(30,66), exterior warp0 and the same gym room/three return warps. The last
+facade row uses the native covered layer so a player standing in front is drawn
+over it; upper roof/tower rows cover a player behind them. Collision follows
+occupied art cells rather than making the transparent tower corners solid.
+
+The first integration retains General door0x03D and its existing animation. It
+looks wooden against the generated glass entrance; a bespoke door and animation
+are a separate visual polish item, not a newly allocated entrance or warp.
+
+## Reproduce and verify
+
+Use a Python interpreter with Pillow installed. The tested local interpreter is
+`/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3`.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/compile_station.py --install
+TAICHUNG_GAME_SOURCE="$PWD" bash ../../scripts/build-game.sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/check_station.py
+python3 -B tools/taichung/validate_city.py --baseline ee75ad0 --json
+```
+
+The compiler writes only its bank; `--install` also patches the96-cell envelope
+and OldCity's secondary label. It does not register C declarations automatically.
+The original required metatile IDs are frozen in `native-source-contract.json`
+so rebuilding after replacement remains deterministic.
+
+The asset check compares all44 retained source-metatile renders and attributes,
+all2784 map cells outside the footprint, the unchanged animated door/approach/
+arrival, all19456 encoded4bpp pixels, sixteen BGR555 palette entries and byte-
+identical regeneration of twenty source files. The city check covers allten
+paired gyms and24 directed seam cells. Runtime entry, return, sprite layering
+and Save/Continue evidence is recorded separately under
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/qa/station-native/`.
