+# National Taichung Theater art study
+
+The user approved the National Taichung Theater silhouette with “Use this
+direction”. Its photo-referenced study now has a deterministic native encoding,
+a prepared Xitun secondary bank and a checked map proposal. Root owns serial C,
+layout and map registration plus emulator validation. No other landmark is
+started by this package.
+
+Ownership follows `city-v2-workstreams.md`. Review delivery follows the latest
+`review-cadence.md`: deliver each ready item independently and promptly, with one
+focused decision per item, without waiting for a bundled review pack.
+
+## Concrete output
+
+`data/taichung/landmarks/theater/` contains `placement.json`, `references.json`,
+`art-brief.md`, the exact `generation-prompt.txt` and measured `generation.json`.
+The built-in `image_gen` output is saved under the root artifact directory as
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/theater-study-v1.png`.
+
+The complete official exterior reference shows the irregular hourglass/bottle
+facade, large glass fields, pale concrete and rectangular mass. The daylight
+close-up supplies material colors. The approved Station image and native game
+screenshot are rendering-style references only. Downloaded official photographs
+stay in isolated artifacts as reference material.
+
+## Native contract boundary
+
+The proposed 16×10-metatile envelope has logical size 256×160 at origin (4,35).
+It preserves baseline door (12,44), local (8,9), exterior warp2 and all three gym
+return bindings. Approach (12,45) and arrival (12,47) remain clear at elevation3.
+Future expanded-city coordinates remain undecided.
+
+The north three art rows are transparent. All 81 Maple street cells at x3..29,
+y35..37 remain byte-identical and walkable. Only the old placeholder facade
+x7..17,y38..44 is restored to plaza paving before foreground compositing.
+Transparent new-envelope cells retain their underlying map word. Painted cells
+are solid, and the lowest facade row uses the COVERED layer type so a player
+standing in front renders in front. Root still needs to check layering in-game.
+
+## Sources
+
+- [Official Theater architecture and design](https://www.npac-ntt.org/en/about/architecture/design).
+- [Taichung Film Assistance: complete exterior photograph](https://filmtaichung.org.tw/index.php/en/scenesContent/162).
+- [Taichung Tourism: official photograph album](https://www.taichung.travel/en/multimedia/album/8044).
+
+The user approved the silhouette with “Use this direction”. The preserved original
+output remains an architectural study. Its measured limitations are recorded in the source metadata;
+The original study keeps `nativeReady=false`; the independently encoded bank
+also remains unregistered until Root completes integration and ROM inspection.
+
+The first output is1536×1024, with60,583 visible RGBA values and255 alpha levels;
+it retains a soft halo. Its height misses the requested1536×960 canvas and none of
+25,477 visible complete aligned6×6 blocks is a uniform logical pixel. The generated
+facade was approved as the architectural direction. The original image is
+preserved unchanged and is not used directly as a source tilesheet.
+
+## Independent native-size candidate
+
+`candidate/` now holds an indexed256×160 bitmap, palette7 candidate, flip-deduplicated
+4bpp graphics, relative foreground tilemap/metatile data and encode/budget manifests.
+The review artifact `landmark-art/theater-native-candidate-v1.png` is an unchanged4×
+nearest display of those native pixels. This candidate has14 opaque colors, binary
+alpha and319 unique8×8 graphics. A1-pixel-cluster trial exceeded capacity at412;
+uniform2×2 clusters preserve the silhouette and reduce that cost.
+
+Read-only analysis of the actual Xitun scene, excluding only the old Theater facade,
+finds20 raw /18 flip-deduplicated secondary graphics, with palette7 unused. The
+combined candidate/remaining-scene bank needs337 graphics. Reserving eight of384
+hardware slots for door animation leaves376 scene slots and39 free before padding.
+Preserving79 source metatile IDs and appending160 candidate cells uses239/384.
+The general-purpose69-graphic prefab catalog is not the actual per-map requirement.
+
+## Prepared native bank and map proposal
+
+`tools/taichung/landmarks/compile_theater.py` prepares
+`data/tilesets/secondary/taichung_xitun/` without an install option. The bank keeps
+the original 79 metatile slots so the 15 IDs used elsewhere in Xitun remain
+stable, zeroes unused source definitions and appends 160 art cells. The resulting
+239 definitions fit the 384-definition limit.
+
+The bank uses 18 flip-deduplicated graphics for the remaining scene plus 319 for
+the Theater: 337 unique graphics, padded to 352 loaded slots in a 128-pixel-wide
+sheet. There are24 immediately unallocated scene slots; another15 padding slots can
+be reclaimed by recompiling. Palette7 holds the 14 opaque Theater colors. All
+other original palette files, including the used palette8/9, remain byte-identical.
+Future neighborhood colors require a fresh scene and palette count. This bank
+does not include every available prefab or promise that a full future kit fits.
+
+`proposal/map.bin` changes 109 cells within the art envelope, leaves all 2,400
+outside cells unchanged and preserves the existing General 0x03D animated door at
+(12,44). That door intentionally replaces one candidate raster cell. The
+`proposal/baseline-map.bin` snapshot permits reproducible encoding after Root
+installs the proposal. No registered map, layout, C declaration or registry was
+changed by these tools.
+
+Run the compiler and `tools/taichung/landmarks/check_theater.py` with the repository's
+Pillow-enabled Python. Checks pass for all 40,960 art pixels, 15 preserved source
+metatile renders/attributes, 2,400 outside-envelope map words/renders, transparent
+ground retention, collision and Maple road paths, fixed warp bindings, 35 source
+hashes and byte-identical rebuilding of 40 files. The repository's actual gbagfx
+converter matches both the generated 4bpp sheet and palette7 binary.
+
+The root artifacts `landmark-art/theater-proposed-{door,arrival,roof}-source.png`
+are 240×160 camera crops of the proposed native source. They show initial
+animation frames without a player or object events and are not runtime captures.
+The companion `theater-proposed-map-source.png` shows the full source map.
+
+Root must register the bank and reviewed map, then test walking/cycling, animated
+entry, all three interior returns and player/roof layering. The approved shape
+does not require another architecture decision.
