@@ -0,0 +1,152 @@
+# Current native minimap map contract
+
+`data/taichung/minimap-contract.json` is the version 1 geometry handoff for the
+live minimap described in the parent project's `docs/navigation-and-bike.md`.
+It covers the registered three-district playable baseline. Main binds this
+geometry to its exact combined ROM and native navigation packet; Interface owns
+rendering/preferences and Gameplay owns fresh native position/context.
+
+The exporter reads `docs/taichung-city-contract.json`, `data/maps/map_groups.json`,
+the actual map JSON files and `data/layouts/layouts.json`. Native group/number
+values follow the same zero-based order as `tools/mapjson/mapjson.cpp`:
+`packedMapId = number | (group << 8)`. Proposed expanded-city coordinates and
+geographic GPS are not inputs to this playable-baseline transform.
+
+## Consumer schema
+
+The main lookup is `mapsByNativeKey[`${group}:${number}`]`. Schema version 1 has:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `world` | 120×120 compressed-world metatiles; bounds `[0,0,120,120]` |
+| `mapsByNativeKey` | Registered exterior/interior map metadata, dimensions and projection policy |
+| `nativeKeysByMapId` | Reverse lookup from native C map constant to `group:number` |
+| `markersById` | Ten stable landmark/gym IDs, EN/Traditional Chinese names, exterior entrances and native gym map IDs |
+| `seams` | Actual native connection offsets, overlap counts and aligned endpoint examples |
+| `plannedMaps` | Explicitly unregistered optional room metadata; excluded from the live lookup |
+| `geometryFingerprintSha256` | Canonical geometry fingerprint for Main's build binding |
+| `sourceSha256` | Exact source inputs used by the exporter |
+| `validation` | Roundtrip, native-ID, marker and seam checks plus one projection example |
+
+`gymId` is the stable landmark string, such as `old-taichung-station`.
+`gymMapId`/`gymNativeKey` identify its actual native room. Numeric badge/save-bit
+assignments remain Gameplay's contract and are not inferred from array order.
+
+Coordinates are integer **metatiles**, 16×16 native pixels each, zero-based,
+**x right / y down**, with north up. Every rectangle uses
+`[minX,minY,maxXExclusive,maxYExclusive]`. Native local coordinates must already be
+unbuffered: `gSaveBlock1Ptr->pos` follows this convention. A publisher using
+object-event virtual map coordinates must subtract `MAP_OFFSET` (currently 7)
+first; the minimap must not silently add/subtract it again.
+
+## Exterior transforms
+
+| Native key | Native map | Dimensions | World origin | World rectangle |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `43:0` | `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY` | 40×72 | `[80,48]` | `[80,48,120,120]` |
+| `43:1` | `MAP_TAICHUNG_GREENWAY` | 40×72 | `[40,32]` | `[40,32,80,104]` |
+| `43:2` | `MAP_TAICHUNG_XITUN` | 40×64 | `[0,0]` | `[0,0,40,64]` |
+
+Check `0 <= localX < width` and `0 <= localY < height`, then compute:
+
+```text
+worldX = worldOrigin[0] + localX
+worldY = worldOrigin[1] + localY
+u = (worldX + 0.5) / 120
+v = (worldY + 0.5) / 120
+```
+
+The normalized coordinates place the dot at the tile's center. For a 160×160
+minimap, native `43:0` at local `[30,66]` becomes world `[110,114]`, normalized
+`[0.9208333,0.9541667]`, or pixel center `[147.3333,152.6667]`.
+
+The 120×120 canvas contains blank regions outside the three exterior rectangles.
+An in-canvas coordinate alone does not establish a playable map. The reverse
+transform requires exactly one covering exterior rectangle; `[0,119]` has none.
+
+## Landmark and interior anchors
+
+Markers use the stable **exterior entrance tile**, rather than the sign, arrival
+plaza, building center or a room's local tile. All ten native gym rooms are
+13×16, with explicit parent mappings:
+
+| Gym native key | Stable ID | Parent exterior | Entrance world |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `43:3` | `old-taichung-station` | `43:0` | `[112,112]` |
+| `43:4` | `taichung-park` | `43:0` | `[112,78]` |
+| `43:5` | `miyahara` | `43:0` | `[100,100]` |
+| `43:6` | `natural-science-museum` | `43:1` | `[64,52]` |
+| `43:7` | `calligraphy-greenway` | `43:1` | `[62,68]` |
+| `43:8` | `shen-ji-new-village` | `43:1` | `[50,76]` |
+| `43:9` | `fine-arts-museum` | `43:1` | `[50,94]` |
+| `43:10` | `fengjia-night-market` | `43:2` | `[24,12]` |
+| `43:11` | `maple-garden` | `43:2` | `[12,32]` |
+| `43:12` | `taichung-theater` | `43:2` | `[12,44]` |
+
+For an interior, first validate the packet's local tile against that room's
+dimensions, then use `parentEntranceWorld` and label the position as indoors.
+Room tiles `[0,0]` and `[12,15]` deliberately yield the same outdoor anchor.
+Interior projection is therefore many-to-one; only exterior projection is
+bijective.
+
+When `docs/station-welcome-map-contract.json` exists, the exporter also reads its
+Station parent marker and separate direct outdoor handoff. Until its native ID
+and layout appear in the actual registry, it stays in `plannedMaps` with
+`nativeKey: null` and `usableForLivePosition: false`; proposed `43:13` is not live.
+After Main registers it, rerun the exporter: the real numeric ID and dimensions
+come from the registry, regardless of the document's proposed-ID/status fields.
+Its minimap anchor is Station entrance `[112,112]`; direct starter handoff lands
+at world `[110,114]`. Those coordinates serve different purposes. This metadata
+does not add a physical welcome-room door or warp.
+
+At this handoff, Main has registered Welcome as **`43:13`, 13×10**. The final
+export therefore has 14 active native mappings and an empty `plannedMaps` list.
+All 14 numeric IDs match the generated `include/constants/map_groups.h`.
+
+## Invalid/stale state
+
+Unknown IDs, non-integer/out-of-bounds local coordinates, missing mappings or
+incompatible schema/build must hide the live location. Do not clamp an invalid
+local tile into a neighboring district or fabricate a coordinate. A transition
+packet can briefly contain an edge coordinate outside normal bounds; suspend
+until Gameplay publishes a valid, coherent field snapshot.
+
+Main must bind `geometryFingerprintSha256` to the exact built ROM and packet
+metadata. A source fingerprint alone does not establish which ROM the browser
+loaded. Interface must also respect native readiness/context/freshness, hiding
+or suspending live minimap output during startup, menus/dialogue, battles,
+loading and transitions. Missing/stale live data must not become a static dot
+presented as a live position; the detailed visitor map remains a separate UI.
+
+## Export and verification
+
+Run from the mapping checkout, or use `--source /path/to/Main/native-checkout`:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/export_minimap.py
+python3 -B tools/taichung/export_minimap.py --check
+```
+
+The first command writes only the JSON export. `--check` reads and regenerates
+in memory, rejecting a stale/edited export. Input fingerprints are checked for
+changes during export so concurrent registration cannot yield a mixed snapshot.
+The exporter never changes native maps, map groups, layout registries, C, scripts
+or browser UI. It needs only Python's standard library.
+
+Validation covers all **8,320** exterior map-local tiles through local→world→local
+roundtrips, reverse native-ID bijection, all ten unique marker/native-gym pairs,
+entrance warps and three authored return warps per gym, indoor parent anchors,
+unknown/out-of-bounds behavior, and every seam edge pair.
+
+The four directed native connections cover **176** aligned edge pairs. Old City
+to Greenway uses native offset `-16`: Old City `[0,20]` at world `[80,68]` connects
+to Greenway `[39,36]` at world `[79,68]`. Greenway to Xitun uses `-32`: Greenway
+`[0,10]` at world `[40,42]` connects to Xitun `[39,42]` at world `[39,42]`. The dot
+moves one world tile across either seam while its transverse world coordinate
+remains unchanged; reciprocal native offsets are checked.
+
+The planned-to-registered welcome behavior was also exercised in an isolated
+temporary registry: a room deliberately registered at `43:14` with dimensions
+14×11 replaced the planned entry and retained the correct Station anchor. This
+confirms that proposal values are not substituted for actual registration;
+the real source registry and room were unchanged by that check.
