@@ -0,0 +1,143 @@
+# OldCity graphics feasibility audit
+
+A scene-specialized primary clone has enough graphics space for the currently
+encoded Station, Miyahara V2, Park and color kit in arithmetic. The explicit
+allowlist leaves 412 unused primary graphic indices. The combined pool requires
+668 new patterns after reuse of a preserved static primary pattern; 412 primary
+holes plus 376 usable secondary slots leave 120 raw slots unallocated.
+
+This is a read-only feasibility result. No clone, graphic assignment, metatile
+remapping or native map change has been created. Runtime correctness remains
+unproven. Exact input hashes, per-input metatile/graphic allowlists and pattern
+pool metadata are in `data/taichung/landmarks/old-core-bank-audit.json`.
+
+## Explicit preservation scope
+
+The raw primary reservation includes every General graphic referenced by:
+
+- All cells and borders of current `TaichungOldCity`, `TaichungGreenway` and
+  `TaichungXitun`, including primary-graphic references inside their secondary
+  metatile definitions.
+- Every module in the complete source prefab catalog.
+- The V4 64×64 filled fixture and its complete block catalog.
+- Every named `METATILE_General_*` definition, providing a conservative closure
+  for common General grass-cut and door replacements.
+- All 70 fixed graphics overwritten by `InitTilesetAnim_General`.
+
+| Primary reservation | Graphics |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Referenced raw indices, including named dynamic definitions | 166 |
+| Fixed animation indices | 70 |
+| Overlap between those sets | 8 |
+| Total reserved indices | 228 |
+| Unreferenced raw indices available to a new clone | 412 |
+
+The audit lists all 412 candidate indices explicitly. It does not move any used
+graphic or require source-entry changes for this raw-hole option. A compiler
+could copy General into a new local primary and replace only those unused slots.
+The global General source must stay unchanged. This scope does not cover other
+maps, future prefabs, new connections or arbitrary metatile replacements.
+
+The General callback writes 416..463, 464..481 and 508..511. These 70 destinations
+stay at their original indices and cannot hold static artwork. A static pattern
+must not share an animated destination merely because its initial frame matches.
+
+## Full-General reference
+
+Preserving every General definition by flip-aware repacking requires 517 static
+patterns plus the 70 fixed animation slots: 587 occupied primary slots and only
+53 free. That approach would also need every affected primary-graphic reference
+in General and secondary definitions remapped. Its available room is insufficient
+for the measured pool: the deficit after those 53 slots and usable secondary is
+239 graphics. The larger 412-hole result depends on the explicit scene allowlist.
+
+## Measured OldCity pools
+
+| Pool | Unique indexed patterns before cross-pool deduplication |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Station | 225 |
+| Miyahara V2 | 152 |
+| Park encoded candidate | 185 |
+| Complete source/color kit | 110 |
+
+The source/color kit is measured from the current complete catalog and recipe
+compiled in memory: 62 source patterns plus 48 colored patterns. Its pattern set
+matches the V4 native color fixture. This is the current recipe count; earlier
+prototype counts are not treated as an allocation. Actually referenced current
+OldCity secondary graphics are included in the union as an additional guard.
+
+All three landmark rasters use the exact same 16-entry Station palette7. The
+source kit retains its existing palette references and colored roofs use 12.
+Graphic deduplication compares indexed patterns including flips; the same index
+pattern can serve different palettes because palette selection belongs to the
+metatile reference. This audit does not merge RGB colors or change any palette.
+
+Station and Miyahara share one pattern. Their union is 376. With Park, the kit
+and current OldCity secondary references, the total union is 669. One pattern
+already exists in preserved nonanimated General graphics, leaving 668 patterns
+to place. The JSON records pool hashes and exact candidate paths.
+
+## Capacity and definition limits
+
+Secondary background graphics physically contain 384 slots. Door animation
+overwrites global graphics 1016..1023, leaving 376 slots for static artwork.
+Station's current bank has 289 unique graphics and 304 loaded sheet slots, so it
+has 87 raw unique slots or 72 slots after its present padding. Appending each
+landmark as a separate full bank is not a valid combined allocation.
+
+The specialized raw-hole option has 788 available slots across primary holes
+and usable secondary. Placing all 668 measured patterns would consume at least
+292 primary holes if secondary were filled to 376. At the other arithmetic end,
+using all 412 primary holes would leave 256 patterns for secondary. Neither is an
+implemented allocation. The 120 remaining slots are not a reserve for unmeasured
+features, and actual references must exclude door scratch even when a sheet has
+padding there.
+
+A separate envelope-only metatile estimate is 79 original secondary slots,
+96 Station cells, 80 Miyahara cells, 96 Park cells and 32 color variants: 383 of 384
+definitions. This is tight and may shrink by omitting empty or duplicate cells.
+Candidate/color IDs currently overlap and require rebasing. Layer attributes,
+background composition, old-ID preservation and actual allocation have not been
+compiled by this audit.
+
+## Dynamic and engine requirements
+
+The raw-hole count becomes usable only after the integrator constrains every
+runtime path that could reference an unpreserved General definition:
+
+- Grass cutting maps General grass/tree-top cells to mowed definitions. All
+  named General labels are included, but other tileset-specific cut mappings
+  require an explicit policy.
+- Scripted `setmetatile` accepts arbitrary IDs. No direct replacement command is
+  present in the scanned Taichung scripts, but transitive specials, future scripts
+  and saved map mutations still require review.
+- The ash effect restores a metatile from runtime arguments. PCs, special floors,
+  escalators and other map-specific animations also perform replacement. They
+  must be unreachable in these exteriors or added to the allowlist.
+- The clone must retain General's callback, all animation destinations, primary
+  palettes 0..6, IDs and attributes needed by allowed General/secondary definitions.
+  Unused General definitions can still reference reclaimed graphic indices and
+  are not safe merely because their numeric IDs remain present.
+- All General graphics used anywhere in the three current exteriors and borders
+  are reserved for connection previews. Neighbor secondary compatibility, map
+  reload/cache behavior, saves and future seams still need native verification.
+- Door animation owns its eight scratch graphics. Walking, cycling, animated
+  entry/returns, field effects and primary/secondary reloads need emulator checks.
+
+Primary field effects that use object sprites do not automatically establish
+background safety; argument-driven background replacement must be considered
+separately. The audit's `engineSafetyClaim` remains false.
+
+## Reproduction and provenance
+
+Run `tools/taichung/landmarks/audit_old_core_primary.py` with Pillow-enabled Python
+after generating the V4 fixture. The tool writes only its audit JSON. Two runs
+matched apart from the requested output path, all 76 input files stayed unchanged,
+and free indices are disjoint from every required graphic and animation slot.
+Park was encoded by the time this audit ran, so its 185 patterns and exact palette
+match are measured rather than estimated. Future dynamic reserves remain unknown.
+
+The separate Miyahara EOL audit is complete. Both candidate palette files already
+use CRLF, both encoders explicitly write CRLF and Git's `*.pal text eol=crlf`
+restores the same bytes at checkout. No RGB/PNG/study bytes changed and no V1
+preservation exception was needed. Both Miyahara format checkers still pass.
