+++ b/docs/old-core-native-checklist.md
@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Old-core native validation and runtime handoff
+
+`tools/taichung/landmarks/check_old_core.py` checks the actual compiled and
+installed shared bank. It reads the compiler manifest and native source bytes;
+it does not import the compiler, write maps, change C/registries, build a ROM or
+open an emulator. Its JSON result fingerprints the manifest and read source set.
+
+```sh
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/landmarks/check_old_core.py --json --self-test
+```
+
+The default inputs are the actual `old-core-native/manifest.json`, the immutable
+audit reference `a155d17`, and Main's opening reference `21c08cb`. Use `--source`,
+`--manifest`, `--audit-reference` and `--opening-reference` for an intentional
+contract revision. The validator prints to stdout only. Root can retain that
+output alongside the exact feature build and ROM hash.
+
+## Static gates
+
+| Gate | Concrete check |
+| --- | --- |
+| Global General stays original | Compare 40 tracked General files to the audit commit; compare the 10 exact working-tree hashes recorded by the audit, including palettes 0–6. Git-normalized text palettes also compare their line contents. |
+| Primary clone preserves live graphics | Compare all 228 protected raw graphic indices pixel-for-pixel, including all 70 fixed General animation destinations. Preserve palettes 0–6, General metatile IDs, the 86 allowed definitions/attributes and the General callback. |
+| Actual bank and C bindings | Resolve C tiles, palettes, metatiles and attribute declarations to the validated bank paths. Check actual sheet/definition capacities, valid layer types, palette indices and every used static graphic reference below 1016. New static art must not reuse a General animation destination. |
+| Shared palette | Compare palette 7 to the exact approved Station palette and both Miyahara V2/Park source rasters. Compare source/color metatiles to the frozen native-color fixture, including palette 12. |
+| Preserved source appearance | Compare rendered pixels and full attributes for the three districts' required General/Pewter IDs, both complete source catalogs and V4 color/infill inputs. |
+| Actual landmark artwork | Decode the real bank's foreground quadrants and compare them to the three approved indexed rasters, including flips and palette selection. Verify roof/front layer attributes, collision words, occupied map cells and the functional General door words. |
+| Stable routes and returns | Use actual source attributes, map collision and elevations for BFS, district connections and all ten gym bindings. The three changed landmarks retain their original door, approach, arrival and three interior return bindings. Reject unpaired active OldCity doors. |
+| Connection previews | Require all three districts to use the compatible shared bank cohort. Compare the actual borrowed connection strips under the viewer's bank, including the engine's 8-column east strip. |
+| Other district preservation | Greenway/Xitun map and border words remain identical to `21c08cb`; compare their rendered RGB and attributes under the new bank. |
+| Current dynamic roots | Resolve all named General C labels/macros and current Taichung script replacements against the protected/defined namespace. Reject an unprotected General ID or a new exterior behavior outside the audited set. |
+| Welcome flow remains Main's | Compare the guide object, transition/resume/frame scripts, graphical-selector hooks, C welcome guards and spawn to `21c08cb`. Preserve map group numbers, welcome group 43/number 13, 65 walkable cells after the guide, clear spawn/front and the direct outdoor anchor. |
+
+The first independent run found 16 colored-metatile preview mismatches: Greenway
+could borrow OldCity's new frontage words while still using its old secondary
+bank. Root corrected the actual layouts to the shared cohort. The repeated check
+then compared 1,530 borrowed strip cells with zero mismatches and confirmed all
+5,448 Greenway/Xitun map/border words and their appearance were unchanged.
+
+The checked bank contains 258 unique secondary graphics, 272 loaded slots and
+299 secondary definitions. The run also compared 1,038 source/catalog/V4
+metatiles, 188 landmark foreground cells, all ten gym bindings, 24 walkable seam
+crossings and 4,871 reachable exterior nodes. These describe the checked source
+snapshot; later compiler changes require another run. The report records actual
+source hashes instead of treating this paragraph as a permanent build claim.
+
+`--self-test` changes private in-memory copies to verify detection of a protected
+graphic corruption, a door-scratch reference and a layer-bit corruption. It
+does not create a second bank or mutate the real files.
+
+Installed infill without a placement manifest still receives actual-ID, native
+attribute, source-color and route checks. The checker does not claim a complete
+prefab paint/mandatory-clear-mask placement proof without those placement inputs.
+Argument-driven engine handlers and saved-map restoration remain explicit
+runtime/review limits; resolving named C roots is not a universal engine-safety
+claim.
+
+## Root's isolated runtime pass
+
+Root owns the feature build and computer-use QA. Use the existing
+`tools/taichung/qa_server.py` with an explicit feature ROM, an mGBA runtime folder
+and an unused local port. Its arguments are `--rom`, `--runtime` and `--port`.
+No canonical ROM or server on port 4184 is part of this validation workstream.
+The server already supplies the required COOP/COEP headers and `no-store`.
+
+The existing `qa.html` harness supports a fresh unique save by default and a
+stable `?qaSave=<token>` for controlled Continue checks. Reload the tab and load
+the rebuilt feature cartridge after a ROM rebuild; an emulator already running
+keeps its old cartridge bytes. Record the exact source/ROM hash and save token.
+
+1. Start a fresh feature save. Confirm the welcome guide and frame-driven
+   introduction appear inside the room, finish a real starter selection and
+   reach OldCity `(30,66)` with controls restored. Check a language switch with
+   actual native text. Source binding parity is already checked; this verifies
+   loading the new outdoor bank during the transition.
+2. Walk and cycle past the Station, Miyahara and Park. Inspect each silhouette
+   and roof/front layering from the south, east and west. Wait long enough to
+   see General water/flower animation; watch for overwritten or flickering
+   landmark/roof graphics.
+3. Enter all three changed gyms through their real doors and return. Inspect
+   the door-opening frames and stable approach/arrival positions. The door
+   animation uses graphics 1016–1023, which static artwork must never reference.
+4. Cross OldCity–Greenway and Greenway–Xitun in both directions. Pause before
+   crossing so borrowed edge previews are visible; recheck after crossing and
+   returning. Verify unchanged neighborhood pixels, palette reloads and walking
+   or cycling control at the seams.
+5. Save/Continue on the isolated feature save near each changed landmark and
+   after a seam crossing. Separately test a save created before this retile;
+   keep that result distinct from a fresh post-retile save. Capture the actual
+   game canvas using the harness's screen-download control, which rejects an
+   all-black capture. A source renderer image is not runtime evidence.
+
+The checker itself does not start a server, use a browser, inspect the canonical
+ROM or mark any of these runtime steps passed.
+
+## Main-owned cache compatibility decision
+
+The map group and existing door IDs stay stable, but the OldCity geometry and
+new secondary metatile meanings have changed. A pre-retile save may restore old
+viewport words over a newly loaded map even when its saved player position is
+valid. Root's bank check cannot establish that Continue invalidates or migrates
+that cache.
+
+Main owns the cache/version migration decision and its verification. This
+workstream flags the need, records `verifiedWithPreRetileContinue=false`, and adds
+no cache hook, save-version allocation or startup rewrite. A successful fresh
+new-game route is not evidence that a pre-retile Continue is compatible.
