+# Old City save version 3
+
+The Old City landmark release shares one compatible primary/secondary tileset pair across Old City, Greenway and Xitun. Continue from versions 1 and 2 takes a full map-load path in any of these three exteriors, avoiding the cached map-view overlay. Existing engine return warps stay intact unless their explicit Old City destination is one of the exact invalidated positions.
+
+Only the 528 previously walkable Old City cells that became invalid relocate, using the nearest verified connected safe cell from `tools/taichung/landmarks/describe_old_core_delta.py`. The 1,268 still-valid old positions remain in place, including 159 whose graphics or map words changed. The six older version-1 Station blockers still return to the verified Station plaza. Interior saves, party, bag, preferences, badge progress and healing checkpoint are preserved. Current and future save versions are untouched.
+
+The const relocation table is bound to baseline map SHA-256 `bbc5e41392f80a572915988c8580fb34ec94d2c8084e7230549fb40da2762fdd` and final map SHA-256 `388a636ab7065ce5213e98654a19c666b85e75f9aa5432be16a2ddb24158364f`. It occupies ROM rather than EWRAM. Regenerate/review it if collision geometry changes.
+
+`bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-save.sh` compiles the real migration implementation and checks every relocation and retained-safe position for both old versions, three-district reloads, explicit/native returns, protected save data, legacy prototypes, untouched vanilla saves, empty parties and current/future versions. These host tests do not substitute for actual Continue verification of the release ROM.
