+# Common level and battle preparation
+
+Taichung's dedicated map group uses level 50 for supported player and trainer
+Pokémon. The short starter grant and ordinary captures/gifts pass through
+the native `GiveMonToPlayer` hook before party/PC storage. They receive native
+stats, full recovery and the same useful presets as Team selections. Eggs and
+unsupported saved species are preserved. No saved variable or version changes.
+
+An accepted gym challenge prepares the chosen party only after the existing
+challenge validator succeeds. `TaichungTeamPrepareParty` restores HP, status
+and PP with the native healing API and applies level-50 presets. Declining,
+invalid preparation and already-completed gyms do not prepare or award a badge.
+The actual trainer start/end callback remains the sole completion writer.
+
+Before a city battle, an older supported party member whose level differs
+from 50 receives a one-time upgrade. Once already level 50, ordinary exploration
+battles preserve its current HP/status/PP. Existing identity, nickname, OT,
+IVs/EVs and held item are retained. Normalization writes the species' correct
+experience-table value, recalculates stats, then explicitly restores HP to
+avoid the original engine's high-to-low-level HP underflow.
+
+City battles skip experience and battle EV awards in `Cmd_getexp`, before
+either gain occurs. This prevents level-up move-learning and automatic
+postbattle evolution. Native city partners obey regardless of Kanto badge
+flags; the ten landmark bits remain independent. Rules outside the dedicated
+city group keep their original behavior. Optional items and manual move
+changes are not prerequisites for a viable freely selected team.
+
+The Station retains its clearly provisional Rattata/Pidgey fixture for this
+mechanics checkpoint, now both level 50 with 31 IVs and curated useful moves.
+This isolates battle/recovery/progression review from the separately proposed
+authored roster, final art and balance. The normal whiteout/checkpoint path
+remains in use: defeat preserves the chosen party and badge mask, heals, and
+returns to the nearby Station plaza, where the challenge can be accepted again.
+Vanilla money-loss feedback still exists; free Team choices never cost money.
+
+`bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-team.sh` compiles the actual team module
+against explicit host engine stubs. It covers capacity, direct evolved picks,
+invalid/battle contexts, item/mail retention, native EXP-table normalization,
+identity retention, downward HP recovery, unsupported/egg guards, no repeat
+exploration refill and unchanged saved preferences/progress. The existing
+`test-progress.sh` independently covers all ten saved bits and every non-win,
+mismatched trainer/start, cancellation and duplicate callback. Native runtime
+evidence is delivered separately; host mocks do not prove a real battle result.
