+# Native Taichung map blockout
+
+Ownership: `feature/city-map`, isolated from the canonical build. This is real
+FireRed map/layout/event data. The reused buildings are provisional blockout
+art; the landmark halls do not implement trainer battles or badges.
+
+`taichung-city-contract.json` is the machine-readable interface for gameplay,
+localization, the visitor guide, and later transport. Coordinates are zero-based
+metatiles (16×16 pixels). Native map group 43 is appended; existing groups and
+map/layout identifiers retain their values.
+
+## Topology
+
+| District | Native map (group, number) | Size | Stitched origin |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Old city / arrival | `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY` (43,0) | 40×72 | (80,48) |
+| Greenway / cultural | `MAP_TAICHUNG_GREENWAY` (43,1) | 40×72 | (40,32) |
+| Xitun / western | `MAP_TAICHUNG_XITUN` (43,2) | 40×64 | (0,0) |
+
+Old city west edge rows20–23 and50–53 join Greenway east rows36–39
+and66–69. Greenway west rows24–27 join Xitun east rows56–59. The
+connections work in both directions and use common primary tiles at the seams.
+Other boundary cells are closed. The two old-city roads permit a loop instead
+of requiring the same street on every journey. Running and cycling are enabled
+throughout the exteriors; doors lead to interiors where cycling is disallowed.
+
+The map is a deliberately nonuniform compression. Miyahara remains near the
+station, the park remains north of them, cultural landmarks form a central
+axis, and Fengjia/Maple Garden/the theater form the western cluster. Buildings
+receive enough space for their doors, signs, paths and future artwork. Most
+ordinary city blocks disappear. The original coordinates in the visitor catalog
+remain the source for the real-world map, rather than these game coordinates.
+
+## Landmark door contract
+
+Every exterior door faces south, uses a native animated door with collision1 /
+elevation0, and enters interior warp1. Its southern approach is clear at
+elevation3. Three interior exit tiles (5/6/7,14) all return to the same exterior
+warp; exiting automatically steps the player onto the clear southern approach.
+
+| Landmark | Exterior | Door / exterior warp | Safe arrival | Interior number |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Old Station | Old city | (32,64) / 0 | (30,66) | 3 |
+| Taichung Park | Old city | (32,30) / 1 | (32,34) | 4 |
+| Miyahara | Old city | (20,52) / 2 | (20,55) | 5 |
+| Science Museum | Greenway | (24,20) / 0 | (24,23) | 6 |
+| Greenway / Civic Square | Greenway | (22,36) / 1 | (22,39) | 7 |
+| Shen Ji New Village | Greenway | (10,44) / 2 | (10,47) | 8 |
+| Fine Arts Museum | Greenway | (10,62) / 3 | (10,65) | 9 |
+| Fengjia Night Market | Xitun | (24,12) / 0 | (24,15) | 10 |
+| Maple Garden | Xitun | (12,32) / 1 | (12,35) | 11 |
+| National Taichung Theater | Xitun | (12,44) / 2 | (12,47) | 12 |
+
+All room IDs and host script/local IDs are in the JSON. Hosts currently stand
+at (6,5) in a shared13×16 lobby. The gameplay owner can replace the room events
+and distinct `TaichungCity_Host_*` script labels after handoff. No new persistent
+variables, badge flags, trainers, species tables, or progression are allocated.
+Habitat rectangles reserve grass and water locations; they do not supply wild
+encounter tables for these new map IDs. Main/gameplay owns that next step.
+
+## Opening, healing and compatibility
+
+Old city references the original shared `Taichung_OnFrame` table for language
+selection, the short welcome and the one-time four-starter/supplies grant. No
+gift logic is copied. Transition and resume call the existing migration for
+legacy prototype saves. Old Pallet/Greenway geometry, tea scripts, interior
+return warps and existing saves are left intact.
+
+The intended new-game spawn is Old city (30,66), elevation3. The one-line
+`src/new_game.c` switch is a separate commit for Main to review/integrate.
+
+The station guide at (28,66) heals on request. Until Main integrates a station
+checkpoint, `TaichungCity_OnTransition` deliberately selects the valid legacy
+Pallet guest-house respawn. That prevents an uninitialized healer reference;
+it is a compatibility fallback, not the final station whiteout behavior.
+
+Three region sections supply short English banners. `MAPSEC_NONE` remains197,
+its baseline value, by placing it explicitly in the JSON before the new
+sections; all old section IDs also stay unchanged. The native Kanto/Sevii
+region-map search is now bounded, so opening it from a custom section cannot
+read beyond the Sevii arrays. Its art remains the legacy Kanto map; the
+Taichung visitor guide is a separate feature owned by the guide stream.
+
+All newly added English script text is in `data/scripts/taichung_city.inc` under
+the prefix `TaichungCity_Text_`; bilingual landmark names are in the contract.
+Localization owns translating these symbols and banner rendering coverage.
+
+## Reproduction and checks
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/taichung/validate_city.py --baseline ee75ad0
