+# Level 50 team presets
+
+The native Team picker supports the contiguous Kanto species constants #001–150, Bulbasaur through Mewtwo. Mew and later-generation species are outside this first roster. `TAICHUNG_TEAM_LEVEL` is 50. The caller creates or normalizes the Pokemon; this module never changes its level, species, identity, held item, stats, HP, status, party slot, language, preferences or badge progress.
+
+`TaichungTeamSpeciesAllowed(species)` checks the roster. `TaichungTeamGetPresetMoves(species)` returns four slots, or `NULL` for an unsupported species. `TaichungTeamApplyPreset(mon)` installs those moves, resets PP Ups and restores each move's base PP through `SetMonMoveSlot`. Unsupported species and a null pointer are left untouched. Empty slots use `MOVE_NONE` and zero PP.
+
+The explicit data lives in `src/data/taichung_team_presets.h`. Each set uses native FireRed level-up moves available by level 50, level-up moves retained from a pre-evolution, or that species' native TM/HM/tutor compatibility. The game grants them directly; obtaining a TM, meeting a tutor, trading, leveling or evolving is not required. The direct evolved-form picker can intentionally create forms such as Dragonite at level 50. No preset depends on Return/Frustration friendship scaling, Hidden Power IV tuning, an egg move, event move, held item or an imported later-generation move.
+
+Useful coverage and straightforward attacks are preferred to competitive optimization. FireRed's type-based physical/special rules still apply. Some species are intrinsically weak and equal levels do not equalize their stats. Sleep, status, setup and recovery moves are deliberate options; this is an initial balance pass. No self-KO or OHKO moves appear in these sets. Manual move editing is separate work.
+
+Six species honestly have fewer than four moves:
+
+| Species | Preset |
+| --- | --- |
+| Caterpie | Tackle, String Shot |
+| Metapod | Tackle, String Shot, Harden |
+| Weedle | Poison Sting, String Shot |
+| Kakuna | Poison Sting, String Shot, Harden |
+| Magikarp | Tackle, Flail, Splash |
+| Ditto | Transform |
+
+Metapod and Kakuna keep their legal pre-evolution attacks so they can act immediately. Ditto uses its native transformation behavior rather than invented attacks.
+
+Run `python3 tools/taichung_gameplay/validate-team-presets.py` in the native checkout. It parses the real species constants, learnsets, evolution links, TM/HM and FireRed tutor tables, and battle move PP/power. The initial pass covers all 150 entries and 590 nonempty move slots; it checks roster completeness, duplicates, packed empty slots, positive PP, legal move sources and a damaging move for every species except Ditto. Initial source counts, preferring level inheritance when a move has several sources: 226 level/inherited slots, 309 TM/HM slots and 55 tutor slots. This source-data validation does not substitute for the caller's ROM build and native picker/battle runtime checks.
