+# Minimal Theater bank integration
+
+Keep `gTileset_TaichungOldCorePrimary` in all three districts and switch only
+Xitun's secondary to `gTileset_TaichungXitun`. The existing Theater bank fits this
+exact scene: 18 retained source patterns plus 319 Theater patterns produce 337
+unique graphics, 352 loaded slots and 239 metatile definitions. The source scene
+and borrowed strips do not use palette 7, so it can hold the approved Theater
+palette without changing surrounding colors.
+
+The reference is the released `d7053fd115b3744b22a2ba3160b4240f5cc80355`, rather
+than a mutable working tree. The read-only reproduction tool is
+`tools/taichung/landmarks/analyze_theater_cohort.py`; its full source hashes,
+per-map usage and results are in
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/theater-analysis/cohort-analysis.json`.
+
+## Exact boundary proof
+
+| Viewer | Donor cells copied by the engine | Cells |
+| --- | --- | ---: |
+| Xitun, right connection with offset 32 | Greenway x0–7, y0–38 | 312 |
+| Greenway, left connection with offset −32 | Xitun x33–39, y25–63 | 273 |
+
+Both sets use only General metatile IDs `0x001`, `0x00E`, `0x00F`, `0x016`,
+`0x017` and `0x175`. No secondary, colored-roof or landmark-private metatile is
+borrowed between Xitun and Greenway. Pixels and full attributes match under both
+secondary banks. Including OldCity–Greenway, all 1,530 directed borrowed-strip
+cells compare identically.
+
+The first conservative calculation included Greenway's entire left strip. That
+included museum facade IDs below row 38 which Xitun never imports; those extra
+13 IDs do not belong to the actual connection contract. The exact clipped proof
+therefore needs no additions to the existing Theater bank.
+
+`LoadMapFromCameraTransition` in `src/overworld.c` copies secondary graphics and
+reloads palette banks 7–12. It does not reload primary graphics. Retaining the
+same primary label is essential. Reverting Xitun to `General` would make its
+declared primary differ from the primary actually resident after a seam crossing.
+
+## Rendering and interfaces
+
+The approved Theater is at origin `(4,35)`, size 16×10 metatiles. The door stays
+`(12,44)`, approach `(12,45)` and arrival `(12,47)`, with exterior warp 2 and all
+existing gym returns. The 81 Maple street cells x3–29, y35–37 remain unchanged.
+The analysis independently compares pixels, attributes and map words outside
+the approved retired-facade and new-ink area.
+
+Root's registered installation is accepted by the old-core checker only through
+the narrowly scoped `shared_cohort` exception. It requires the released-baseline
+installation manifest, unchanged shared primary bytes, unchanged district event
+and warp interfaces, preserved surrounding pixels/attributes and the exact
+installed map hash. The separate existing connection-strip gate still compares
+the actual banks in both directions. OldCity/Greenway's bank and the existing
+old-core graphics, landmark, route and welcome checks remain in force.
+
+There is no reason to merge the full Theater art into the already allocated
+OldCore bank for this increment. Such a merge would require another allocation
+and resolution of the two different palette-7 meanings. Exact reuse of current
+nonanimated primary patterns could reduce a rebuilt Theater secondary to 318
+patterns, but it is unnecessary for the safe 337-pattern installation.
+
+## Separate save-position caveat
+
+No map number, door, warp or save structure needs to change for the bank switch.
+That does not establish compatibility for every old saved position: the approved
+new silhouette blocks 33 previously open Xitun cells around the old facade.
+Their coordinates are recorded in the analysis JSON. Released save version 3
+skips the existing upgrade path for already-version-3 saves.
+
+Main owns the resulting v4 position/cache migration decision and verification;
+Root has already been alerted. This analysis edits no save code and does not
+claim a pre-Theater Continue test. Native loading, door animation and actual
+game screenshots remain Root's runtime integration work.
